Number = {6},
Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {Among the problems resulted from the continuous urbanization process,
   inefficient urban mobility and high pollution levels have been complex
   challenges that have demanded a lot of public investments and research
   efforts. Recently, some alternative transportation means have been
   leveraged as sustainable options for such challenges, which has brought
   bicycles to a more relevant setting. Besides the sometimes obvious
   benefits of adopting bikes for transportation, technologies around the
   Internet of Things (IoT) paradigm have been advocated as important
   supportive tools to boost smart cycling initiatives. Actually, new
   technologies can be exploited to improve the efficiency of bike paths
   and parking spots, while reducing accidents and enhancing the cycling
   experience of the users. Therefore, in this highly vibrating scenario,
   this article facilitates the understating of current research trends and
   promising developments, surveying and classing recent works. Since there
   is a global interest for the promotion of cleaner and more sustainable
   solutions in large cities, this survey can be valuable when supporting
   new developments in this highly relevant research area.},
